From: Jacob Oursland <jacob.oursland@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 24 Jul 2026 11:30:28 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 148/197] Gui: Close combo popup on the main property-editor
 rebuild path

The prior combo-popup UAF fix (a95c5c0e48) closed the enum QComboBox
drop-down in releaseEditorFocus(), but only wired it into the delaybuild
(commitData) and rowsAboutToBeRemoved paths. The main selection/recompute
rebuild -- PropertyEditor::buildUp() -> PropertyModel::buildUp() -- reaches
the model reset directly and destroyed the persistent combo editor without
calling it.

When an enum combo has its drop-down open (auto-opened by the delegate on
FocusIn) and a rebuild fires, the popup window is freed without Qt's normal
closePopup() teardown. A queued window-system mouse release is then delivered
to the dead popup and routed back into QComboBoxPrivate::itemSelected() on the
dangling combo box, crashing with EXC_BAD_ACCESS in doActivate() <-
emitCurrentIndexChanged() (sender = freed QComboBox).

Call releaseEditorFocus() right before the model reset in buildUp() so this
path also closes the popup and moves focus off the editor while it is still
alive. releaseEditorFocus() early-returns when there is no active editor, so
it is a safe no-op on the common case.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (claude-opus-4-8)
Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5 (claude-opus-5)
---
 src/Gui/propertyeditor/PropertyEditor.cpp | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/Gui/propertyeditor/PropertyEditor.cpp b/src/Gui/propertyeditor/PropertyEditor.cpp
index e2d0bbf67..2f81f7ae8 100644
--- a/src/Gui/propertyeditor/PropertyEditor.cpp
+++ b/src/Gui/propertyeditor/PropertyEditor.cpp
@@ -754,6 +754,10 @@ void PropertyEditor::buildUp(PropertyModel::PropertyList&& props, bool _checkDoc
     //
     // closeTransaction();
 
+    // The model reset below destroys every persistent editor: close an open combo
+    // popup and move focus off the editor first. No-op when nothing is being edited.
+    releaseEditorFocus();
+
     QModelIndex index = this->currentIndex();
     QStringList propertyPath = propertyModel->propertyPathFromIndex(index);
     if (!propertyPath.isEmpty()) {
